    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.26.0</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:42:39 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22600</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.26.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Settings has a Devices page, not a pairing page: the iPhones and browsers signed in to your account, how each got here, and Remove. "Pair an iPhone..." and the QR sheet are gone, and so is the note that pairing always waits for you.</li><li>Your own iPhone or browser joins by signing in with the same account. "Ask before adding my own devices" now means one click: a notification with Approve, or Settings &gt; Devices. There is no code to compare.</li><li>Setting up Squeak no longer shows a QR code for the phone step on Squeak's cloud; it says to sign in on your iPhone. The QR step stays only for an install still on its own server.</li><li>A Mac can't be flooded with new device keys: it adds at most five of your own devices a minute.</li><li>A chat that fails to start now leaves its reason in Squeak's log, and stopping a chat ends its agent process instead of leaving it behind.</li><li>Quitting Squeak puts the Mac's sleep, fans and frozen apps back even if one step is slow, and logs which step was.</li><li>The New chat project list opens faster, no longer waiting on git.</li><li>Squeak writes less to the cloud while you watch a working chat, and re-checks less often while its live connection is healthy.</li><li>The old shared server and the Conductor relay test add-on are gone; no setting changes.</li><li>A chat waiting on Claude says "Waiting for Claude" instead of a stuck "Thinking...".</li><li>Very large chats offer Compact or Continue in a new thread, and compact automatically at 200k tokens.</li><li>A dropped connection shows a clear failure with Try again.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.25.1</h4><ul><li>A working chat no longer jitters: its steps stay on screen and only grow until the reply lands.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.25.0</h4><ul><li>The pond page no longer flashes "Refreshing" or stutters while it updates.</li><li>A pond's accent colour now matches its logo.</li><li>New thread always opens on a live stream, so the first message never goes nowhere.</li><li>Any chat can be archived: "Stop and archive" stops a running chat first.</li><li>A chat with ducklings still running shows as working.</li><li>The pond page lists every thread, including Main and older ones.</li><li>Ponds are projects: there are no more separate branch ponds.</li><li>Calmer connection status: it no longer flickers between states.</li><li>Live Thinking and tool steps show while Claude works.</li><li>No false "Trouble connecting" when the service is briefly slow.</li><li>Main shows in the sidebar only while it has threads, and is labelled Main.</li><li>Streams no longer blink out of the sidebar.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
